<section class="section process" aria-labelledby="esa-title">
  <div class="wrap split">
    <div class="a">
      <p class="label slide"><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>The ESA process</p>
      <h2 id="esa-title" class="display-2 reveal">A permanent record for your home.</h2>
      <p class="lede reveal mt-6" >This is the path each notified job follows, from first wire to final sign-off.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="b timeline" data-stagger>
      <li><h3>Notification filed</h3><p>We file a notification of work with ESA before the job begins. It creates a permanent record of the work at your address.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Staged inspections</h3><p>ESA inspects at key stages such as service, rough-in and final, checking the installation against the Ontario Electrical Safety Code.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Certificate of Acceptance</h3><p>When the work passes, ESA issues a Certificate of Acceptance. Keep it: insurers and future buyers may ask for it.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

